# ti.cc2652r1.freertos_demo
# Real, hand-written (no vendor SDK/generator - see target.toml) FreeRTOS
# (CMSIS-RTOS v1) demo for TI SimpleLink CC2652R1 - reuses the exact same
# real ARM_CM4F kernel/port bundle as tm4c123/freertos_demo's own (both
# chips are genuine Cortex-M4F cores - see this demo's own Makefile
# comment). See
# ../../../../../replica-server/renoly_examples/ti/cc2652r1/README.md.

using sysbus
mach create "CC2652R1_FreeRTOS_Demo"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platform.repl

# Bare @$ORIGIN/firmware.elf - REQUIRED, not stylistic, same real reason
# as every other demo's sim.resc in this repo. A synced flat firmware.elf
# copy lives at this demo's own root (sibling to this file).
sysbus LoadELF @$ORIGIN/firmware.elf

# UART0 DR write watchpoint - observes uartTask's marker/heartbeat bytes.
# is_byte_tap -> Bus Traffic, matching every other UART example.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x40001000 4 Write "print(chr(value & 0xFF), end='')"

# GPIO DOUTTGL31_0 write watchpoint, firing only when the real LED bit
# (DIO7, 0x80 - the green LED on the real CC26X2R1 LaunchPad) is set -
# direct proof defaultTask's blink loop genuinely toggles the real
# onboard LED pin via a real, running FreeRTOS task. Not a byte-tap ->
# lands as a real, labeled [GPIO] Event.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x400220B0 4 Write "if value & 0x80: print('[GPIO] DIO7 toggle value=0x%X' % (value & 0x80))"

# RF Core (BLE stub) CMDR write watchpoint, firing only for pointer-format
# radio-op command submissions (real 2-LSB encoding, bit0 clear) - direct
# proof bleTask genuinely drove the RF Core stub through its real
# boot->CMD_RADIO_SETUP->CMD_BLE_ADV->CMD_BLE_SLAVE sequence. Not a
# byte-tap -> lands as a real, labeled [BLE] Event.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x40041000 4 Write "if not (value & 1): print('[BLE] RF Core command submitted (pointer=0x%08X)' % value)"

start
